The LBL high-temperature downhole flowmeter can be used for the following purposes:
1) Locating production and injection zones [S1][S2];
2) Indicating changes in production and injection zones resulting from acidizing or fracturing [S1];
3) Locating the flashpoint or bubble point in a wellbore [S1][S4];
4) Reflecting scale buildup, casing damage, plugged perforations, or thief zones [S1];
5) Acting as a very sensitive production mode borehole caliper [S4].
